          "problem": "The section states without qualification that a Schedule II prescription from an out-of-state practitioner who holds no M.G.L. c. 94C registration can be filled in Massachusetts only under s. 18(d) or s. 18(d1/2), and only if it was issued within the preceding five days. Section 18(d1/2) contains two later provisos under which a Massachusetts retail pharmacy may fill a narcotic Schedule II prescription without that five-day sentence applying: one for prescriptions received by mail or commercial carrier and delivered to a verified address in the out-of-state residence of the patient, and one for patients admitted to a long-term care facility in Maine or a contiguous state, delivered by a courier employed or contracted by the pharmacy. Neither proviso carries a five-day issue-date condition.",
